{title: Stepping in the Light}
{artist: Eliza E. Hewitt / William J. Kirkpatrick}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: C}
{key_original: Db}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Pentecostal Hymns Nos. 1 and 2 Combined, by Henry Date (Chicago, Illinois: Hope Publishing Company, 1894), # 412)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Trying to walk in the steps of the Savior,
[C]Trying to follow our Savior and [G]king;
[C]Shaping our lives by His [F]blessèd example,
[C]Happy, how [F]happy, the [G7]songs that we [C]bring.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]How [F]beautiful to walk in the [C]steps of the Savior,
[G7]Stepping in the light, [C]stepping in the light,
[C]How [F]beautiful to walk in the [C]steps of the Savior,
[G7]Led in paths of [C]light.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Pressing more closely to Him who is leading,
[C]When we are tempted to turn from the [G]way;
[C]Trusting the arm that is [F]strong to defend us,
[C]Happy, how [F]happy, our [G7]praises each [C]day.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Walking in footsteps of gentle forbearance,
[C]Footsteps of faithfulness, mercy, and [G]love,
[C]Looking to Him for the [F]grace freely promised,
[C]Happy, how [F]happy, our [G7]journey a[C]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Trying to walk in the steps of the Savior,
[C]Upward, still upward, we follow our [G]guide;
[C]When we shall see Him, the [F]King in His beauty,
[C]Happy, how [F]happy, our [G7]place at His [C]side.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
